Patch 3011: the tick-locked audio's output changes speed without changing pitch (WSOLA time stretch in place of the linear resampler; AUDIO_LOCK_STRETCH=0 turns it off).

Why: the output plays at a rate of 0.55 to 1.1 (3007 feedback, 3008 feed-forward, 3009/3010 slow pace and refill), and the linear resampler moved the
pitch with it: a 3010 refill at +6.25 % was a semitone flat, the slow pace at 0.6 almost a fifth.

Output only (blocks mixed, read index and notify events are exactly as in 3005; the 12 ms concealment, the gap line and every 3007-3010 counter are
unchanged; with AUDIO_LOCK_STRETCH=0 the output is 3010's, byte for byte):
- each block's input goes into a static ring (4096 frames); grains of 480 frames (10 ms, periodic Hann) are overlap-added every 240 output frames,
  each one's input start moving by 240 x the rate from the last nominal start, then up to 200 frames (4.2 ms) either way to where it best continues
  the grain before (normalised cross-correlation of the overlap on L+R: every 4th offset on every 2nd frame, then +-3 at every frame);
- at rate 1 the output is the input sample for sample; the ring holds about 9 ms more delay than 3010 (the device level control is unchanged);
- a block puts out 0, 1 or 2 grains (240 frames each); a concealment goes on until a block has real frames, then crossfades as before; a refill's
  debt (3010) is paid by the output frames over the input consumed;
- no allocation, no lock: every buffer is static, the work is on the mix thread: about 50-80 us per burst on the test PC;
- the "[audio-lock]" line keeps every field and appends "time stretch: N grains, pitch-preserving (WSOLA)|off, linear resampler (...)";
- tests: libs/audio/tests/test_audio_lock_race.c part 7 drives the real lk_submit_block on a fake device that records what it gets: a 440 Hz sine
  stays at 440 Hz at rates 0.6, 1/1.0625 and 1.032 (the linear resampler gives 264, 414 and 454), its purity per 100 ms stays over 0.999, the largest
  sample-to-sample step stays at the sine's own (no click at a grain or block join), a 0.2-4 kHz chirp likewise, the length is input / rate; rate 1
  is the input exactly; CPU per burst; part 6's fights with it on (no more gaps than without). Parts 1-6 run with AUDIO_LOCK_STRETCH=0 (3010's
  numbers). AUDIO_LOCK_WAV_DIR=dir writes a test signal (an arpeggio, a vibrato tone, clicks, a chirp) before and after 0.6 and 1.0625, linear and
  WSOLA. audio_lock_measure.c prints the output's CPU per burst.

